    "architectural_insight": "Across all PCIe/Ethernet fabrics (<= 54 GB/s), CFG2-based hybrid forms (cfg2, cfg2sp2, cfg2sp4) strictly dominate pure Ulysses SP because CFG2 cuts per-rank all-to-all volume by 4x at the same GPU count while remaining bitwise-exact on 2 GPUs. Dual-stream block interleaving (SP4i/SP8i) shifts the communication-bound roof down by 2.1x, allowing SP8i to approach CFG2xSP4 once per-rank bandwidth exceeds 40 GB/s (PCIe Gen5 / NVLink).",
